From 9175e774cdd26e118026d75ef2adde0df56c2cf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:27:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Sun shadows: cascades that follow the camera, as Wind Waker
 HD's

The cascades were fixed to the sun and resized from HD's live splits every frame, and the facing term faded out from
12,000 units, so a far island (the title screen's) showed flat until the camera came near. Now, with the "hd" shadow
quality: light space turns with the camera (its right made flat to the sun, as HD's), each cascade is fitted to its
slice of the view (near to split 0, split 0 to 1, split 1 to 4,500, 4,500 to 14,000), its size held in steps of
2^(1/4) with a margin before it shrinks and its centre snapped to whole texels; the terrain mix's fades follow the
live splits by HD's rule; a far fade to lit from 12,000 to 14,000; and the facing term no longer fades with distance
(HD's per-vertex N.L doesn't). DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_CASCADES_FOLLOW=0 keeps the old cascades, to compare.

On Linux: the title's island is shaded from its first frames; the sword state is bit-identical; Link on the pier
within 0.3/255; GPU time the same with three cascades, about 0.1 ms for the fourth.
